2026-09-27T11:25:10.6100884Z Update Note
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6102759Z ===========
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6104534Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6104973Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6105132Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6105534Z ================
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6105732Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6105984Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6106563Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6106897Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6107080Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6107513Z ====================================
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6107788Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6107995Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6108814Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6109367Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6110365Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6111193Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6111362Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6112066Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6112916Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6113416Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6113891Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6114533Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6114665Z Packages
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6114972Z ========
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6115135Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6117162Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6119566Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6119929Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6120678Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6121956Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6122930Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6123773Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6124420Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6197027Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6197250Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6197713Z ==========================
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6197990Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6199958Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6201893Z 
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6202958Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6204270Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T11:25:10.6204596Z 
